        "evidence": "descent-involution-su2.md:19-21: \"we have $\\hat\\tau^2=\\hat\\tau$. That is, $\\hat\\tau$ is a projection, not only an involution of order 2.\"",
        "notes": "An idempotent (τ²=τ) is in general NOT an involution of order 2 (which means τ²=id); the phrasing 'not only an involution' wrongly implies projection is a strengthening of involution. The averaging operator is a projection; calling the block 'descent involution' and asserting it is 'an involution of order 2' is at best loose. The math (averaging is idempotent) is correct; the involution/projection conflation is a wording slip."
      }
